# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The repo root .gitignore carries the standard virtualenv rules `env/` and
# `ENV/` (root .gitignore:154,156), which would swallow this project's entire
# environment directory. A deeper .gitignore wins, so reclaim it first --
# before any other rule -- and let the specific exclusions below apply inside.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!/env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python / tooling caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Keys live in a .env that is parsed in Python, never sourced: the
# '|' in a Mapillary key is a shell pipe.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Endpoint configs. These hold live gradio.live tunnel URLs, which are
# publicly reachable by anyone holding them, and this repository is public.
# board_models.json is the exception: it names public providers only (checked
# -- no keys, no tunnels) and is needed to reproduce the frontier board.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
models.json
*_models.json
*.local.json
.one_model.json
!eval/board_models.json
!models.example.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Panorama imagery and harvested metadata: 24 GB of runtime cache, all
# re-fetchable from the committed task index / the Storage Bucket.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
env/data/panos/
env/data/pool/
env/data/geo/detail/
env/data/geo/osm_cache/

# The training index is ~20 MB and lives in the Storage Bucket beside the
# imagery. The eval index stays committed: a frozen benchmark belongs in
# version control, where a change to it is visible in review.
env/tasks/train_pano_v3.jsonl
env/tasks/pool_offline_5k.jsonl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Collected rollouts and the Remotion video renderer. Both are local working
# material: kept on disk, deliberately never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rollouts/
env/rollouts/
video/
env/video/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw eval episodes: 1.3 GB across 59 arms. The derived per-arm summaries in
# results/ are committed instead -- those are what the reports cite.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/raw/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-run write-ups and session journals: 3,600 lines of working notes kept on
# disk, deliberately not committed. What they establish that a reader needs is
# in LEARNINGS.md and REPRODUCE.md; the HF Jobs notes are published separately.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reports/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local training and simulation output. `grpo_geoguesser.py` and
# `simulate_rollout.py` write here when OUTPUT_ROOT is not a mounted bucket.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/

# The release blog, still in draft.
blog.md
